@startuml
title Flames of War V4 Calculator — system context
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

actor User
rectangle "Flames of War Combat Calculator" {
  component "Streamlit application\n(app.py navigation)\nIMPLEMENTED" as App
  component "Normal Shooting\nview → controller → legacy model\nIMPLEMENTED: abstract binomial chain" as Normal
  component "Artillery Shooting\nview → controller → exact state engine\nIMPLEMENTED: bounded Infantry model" as Artillery
  component "Artillery policy registry\nUS / UK / Japan supported options" as Policies
}
database "NumPy\nnormal simulation + presentation stats" as NumPy

User --> App : select calculator / enter facts
App --> Normal : Normal Shooting route
App --> Artillery : Artillery Shooting route
Normal --> App : legacy CombatResult
Artillery --> Policies : selected Shooting Nation
Policies --> Artillery : verified policy operations
Artillery --> App : per-shooting probability summaries
Normal --> NumPy : binomial simulation
App --> NumPy : normal view histograms / statistics

note bottom of Normal
Existing normal behavior remains a separate legacy calculator.
No V4 direct-fire resolver is implemented by this path.
end note

note bottom of Artillery
Exact probability-state transitions cover a user-entered
finite horizon; no random sampling is used in the domain.
The model is limited to an Infantry target Unit and one battery.
ToT on a Repeat and unlisted weapon/nation rules are unavailable.
end note
@enduml
